  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Either threshold suffices",
      "items": [
        "Standard Genesis capital and leverage interest are each compared independently against the minimum success threshold",
        "The two are never added together; either one meeting the threshold makes Genesis succeed",
        "Preorder funds and leverage debt principal do not count toward the threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Advances take a transaction",
      "items": [
        "Apart from the protection window's automatic resume, every phase advance takes a public transaction to trigger",
        "Unlock time = Genesis deadline + 365 days (fixed); entering Locked early does not change it",
        "The 24-hour protection window counts from the transaction that actually enters Unlocked"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Two exits",
      "items": [
        "Either threshold met: enters Locked, four pools deployed",
        "Neither threshold met: enters Refund, everything refunded in full, no one loses principal",
        "Steady state is the terminal state after unlock completes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "How to read the map",
      "items": [
        "The emphasized rail behind the phase boxes is the timeline backbone, not a direct transition",
        "Faint frames mark the three lanes; labelled arrows are real transitions; the dashed arrow is the failure exit"
      ]
